WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.600
I'm definitely gonna be the first star idol one day!

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.610
Nijino Yume's about to start her Aikatsu!

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.240
So far on Aikatsu Stars!

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:17.370
I'm a second-year exchange student at the idol middle school, Venus Ark.

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:20.040
I work my hardest at Aikatsu every day!

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:26.830
Elza-san's right-hand girl, 
Kizaki Rei-san, is an expert at kendo.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:31.340
Mahiru-chan, who's just as good at karate, 
surprised us all by challenging her to a fight.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:37.050
So many different things have been happening that I can't contain my excitement!

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:39.930
I wonder what fun things'll happen today!

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:46.600
Today's steak is an Okinawan-brand original, Ishigaki beef.{uh, this is word weird but}{I have literally no idea which of us wrote this comment because we basically have the same style. I could be replying to myself for all I know}

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:48.770
What are your impressions?

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:50.400
It's quite good.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.070
Elza-sama!

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:56.240
Kirara's got an off day for the first time in a super duper long time!

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:03.000
FuwaFuwa Dream has kept you rather occupied lately. Take this opportunity to relax and recharge.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.080
Come and sightsee with me, Elza-sama!

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:08.250
That does sound intriguing.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:12.880
However, do you really believe that Elza's schedule would allow for that, Kirara?

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:15.970
What? Then what about you, Rei-chan?

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:19.510
Unfortunately, it's the same for me. 
Go have some alone time.

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:21.640
It's boring by myself!

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.180
Rei, it's time.

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:30.190
Geez, that's so...

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:36.610
I'm sure Elza-sama could've spared <i>some</i> time to play with me...

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:39.070
Finally finished.

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:42.080
Elzacise is crazy hard.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:45.910
You two are incredible though. You're keeping up with the others already.

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:48.290
We're just barely making it.

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:50.670
Yume, it's about time to head out.

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.210
Oh, you're right.

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:54.340
You have plans for today?

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:59.010
Yeah, Rola and I have got a job together again for the first time in a while.

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.140
Check this out.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.510
It's a variety show called "It's the weekend! Where to?"{consider "It's the weekend! Where to?" weil kurz vielleicht besser ist}

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:08.100
We go around Kirakira City as reporters and hit up all the hot spots. {can't remember if this is how we spelled it, there should be a mention in episode 46 or so with Ako}{I can't imagine us spelling it any other way}{I think it was Kira Kira actually, but fuck it}

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:10.400
That sounds like fun!

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.940
Yeah, like a super whole lot of fun! {qc pass fix, I'll be adding super everywhere}

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:14.070
Kirara-chan?

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:17.780
That's it! Kirara's coming too!

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:24.490
It'll be Bring-Kirara-to-Work Day! {"It'll be Bring-Kirara-to-Work Day!"}{YOTO}

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.680
Where should we start?

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.890
Oh, how about the aquarium?

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:08.640
Kirara-chan, we're not here to play.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:11.270
That's right. This is work for us.

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:15.020
But Kirara wants to know more about you two.

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:20.280
You know how funny Ako-chan from S4 is?

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:24.360
I figured the other idols from Four Star might be just as interesting!

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:28.410
Good morning, Yume-chan and Rola-chan.

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:30.200
Let's make a good show today.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.790
Yes, we'll do our best.

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:33.460
Looking forward to it!

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:36.290
Sure, same here... uh, and you are?

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:38.340
I'm Hanazono Kirara.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:39.550
Kiraran!

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:43.930
Aren't you an idol from Venus Ark? Why are you here?

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:46.430
I came to watch!

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:51.270
But sitting on the sidelines sounds boring, so maybe I'll join in and report too!

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:56.310
Won't you let me?

00:04:57.230 --> 00:05:00.360
Nice! Okay, we'll see how it goes.

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:06.660
First up is the food report. {wow, not gourmet report? also consider restaurant report for allit}{wow?}

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:08.030
Food report?

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:10.870
We give our opinions on the food they serve.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:12.750
That sounds easy!

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:16.120
We'll hit the ground running. Three, two... {let's get right into it}{the more times a thing is, the freedomer you can it}

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:19.210
Yume!

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:20.130
Rola!

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:21.500
And Kirara's...

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:24.550
It's the weekend! Where to?

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:28.140
Today, we're at the highly acclaimed Kira Café.

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:29.890
Today we'll be introducing...

00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:32.640
Our shop's pride and joy, the special parfait.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:35.690
It looks delicious!

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:37.690
The fruit is overflowing!

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:39.650
I can't wait another second.

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:41.400
Thanks for the treat.

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:45.950
The cream is so light and airy!

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:48.110
It looks incredible!

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:49.320
Now for the test.

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:51.700
That was yummy!

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:56.910
Right, let's stop rolling.

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:59.670
You can't just down it all like that.

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:00.750
It's baaad?{...}

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:04.300
Food reports always begin with your impression of the visuals.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:07.470
Then you hold it up for the camera before your first bite.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:10.340
After that, you give specific thoughts on it.

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:12.430
Specific thoughts?

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:14.100
For instance...

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:23.610
The thick and rich cream creates a heavenly harmony with the sourness of the berries!

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:26.900
They say the name parfait comes from the word perfect,

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:30.570
but I would go so far as to call this parfect!

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:32.330
That was super amazing!

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:33.700
You're the best, Rola.

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.750
It's only natural.

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:38.290
Keep that in mind and take it from the top.

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:44.300
It's delicious!

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:47.170
The cream is so thick and rich...

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:50.590
It creates a heavenly harmony with the sourness of the berries!

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:53.640
You've gotta come and try this perfect parfait, or else...

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:55.600
Baa!

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:58.230
We've reached our next stop.

00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:01.350
We'll show you this bouldering studio.{1) stop being so japanese 2) did you know that ian has taken up bouldering}{that's very aikatsu of him. is he still in China?}

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:07.230
Bouldering is a sport where you climb up a rock wall without using a rope. {and harness}

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:09.700
Cool, I think we should give it a try ourselves.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:11.240
Yay!

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:15.120
It's no fun just climbing up normally, so let's make it a race!

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:16.660
No, that's too dangerous.

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:18.250
Ready, start!

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:19.160
Wait!

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:23.500
Just try and catch me!

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:26.380
Get back here!

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:30.010
Aikatsu! Aikatsu!

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:36.720
A-As you can see, bouldering uses your entire body, so it's perfect if you want to get in shape.

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:38.470
...katsu!

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:42.770
Aikatsu! Aikatsu!

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:44.400
Yahoo!

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:49.530
That concludes our bouldering experience.

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:51.320
Okay, we're good.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:52.780
Nice!

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:01.540
Wow!

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:03.290
Now it's Kirara's turn!

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:27.860
You three have made this an incredible show.

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:29.940
I'm looking forward to the rest.

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:31.150
Okay!

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:35.570
Kirara-chan, you had me worried at first because of how unconstrained you are.

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:37.780
This whole job gets me going. {I messed up at first, by roke she means the entire thing}{I would have same confused}

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:39.660
I know, right? {futari nara saikyou... or bouken...}

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:43.290
But it would just be baa if I was by myself.

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:45.960
Same if we were all alike.

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:49.920
True, each place is made more fun because Rola's so reliable.

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:52.470
Rola, when did you ever find the time to prepare? {practice}

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:54.840
I didn't really do much beforehand.

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:57.220
I just so happened to get all this stuff right.

00:08:57.550 --> 00:09:00.680
I seem to remember hearing something from the deck last night...

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:05.730
You always put in the effort.

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:10.110
Enough of that. It's time to move.

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:12.530
Next is what we've been waiting for.

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:14.610
The last recording spot.

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:20.870
It looks like a normal park. 
What's so good about this place?

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:21.950
Right over there.

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:26.330
A stage!

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:34.170
Starting today, they're having a weekly 
Weekend Kirakira Stage event here for new idols.

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:39.550
And producing it is an old upperclassman of ours.

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:42.600
It's nice to see you again, Nijino, Sakuraba.

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:46.520
Tsubasa-senpai!

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:51.320
Tsubasa-senpai!

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:52.940
It's been so long.

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:55.190
Have you been well?

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:59.070
I was worried when I heard you were doing an exchange at Venus Ark.

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:00.870
We're making it through somehow.

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:03.740
Sakuraba, Yuzu's told me everything.

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:07.620
You're doing well supporting her as student council vice president. {can't remember caps, I think it was ep 53}{shouldn't need to}

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:12.750
Actually having to do it has made me painfully aware of how tough it was on you.

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:16.380
And considering Yuzu's the president, it must be twice as hard.

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:18.090
You're telling me!

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:21.260
I mean—no, not at all!

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:25.980
Hello, have you two forgotten about Kirara?

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:31.980
Well, this is our senpai from school, Kisaragi Tsubasa-san.

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:35.650
I'm Hanazono Kirara from Venus Ark. Kiraran!

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:37.570
Nice to meet you, Tsubasa-chan!

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:38.950
"Tsubasa-chan"?!

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:47.120
Kirara can see the sparklies just 
shooting off you, Tsubasa-chan! {this is like the fifth unique use of kira kira this episode}

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:48.120
Sparklies?

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:49.000
Yeah!

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:52.330
Oh, but I guess not as much as Elza-sama.

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:55.460
Sh-She doesn't mean any harm.

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:58.260
She just says whatever comes to mind.

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:04.050
Rumors said that Venus Ark was a collection of idol pirates,

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:07.020
but my worries were misplaced if they have girls like her.

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:12.520
Idol pirates? That sounds so cool!

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:15.230
We'll begin with the interview.

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:17.150
And we're rolling!

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:21.780
There are a few questions we'd like to ask Kisaragi Tsubasa-san.

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:25.160
What inspired you to produce this event?

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:31.540
I've always thought that there weren't enough stages for new idols to use.

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:35.290
I wanted to give the up-and-comers more opportunities.

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:37.710
That's a wonderful aspiration!

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:40.800
Why did you choose to make it an open-air stage in the park?{longhood}

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:47.010
Because here, it would be easier to attract people who just so happened to be passing through the park.

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:48.520
What a good idea!

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:52.900
It's got a super great atmosphere! Kirara wants to sing up here too! {I hope she doesn't make meccha a thing}

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:59.530
You can do more than sing—we plan to hold plays, fashion shows, and dance exhibitions too.

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:01.320
Join in if you get the chance.

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:05.030
And now you know all about the Weekend Kirakira Stage.

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:07.120
Please come check it out!

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:10.830
And cut! Okay, very nice!

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:15.580
All that's left is to report on the concert this evening, and we're done.

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:21.170
The concert's going to be held by the Four Star Academy first-years who passed that recent audition, right?{are we really going to just say Four Star in general now}{only when I feel like it}

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:28.060
Yeah, we're having them self-produce and do the stage decorations, seating arrangements, and everything else.{I thought you were the producer, Tsubasacchi}

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:30.470
They should be arriving soon...

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:32.180
Kisaragi!

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:34.730
Anna-sensei!

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:39.110
Nijino, Sakuraba, I guess you were the interviewers today...

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:40.030
Yes.

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:42.490
More importantly, did something happen?

00:12:43.570 --> 00:12:44.990
We have an emergency.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:03.760
What do you mean they're going to be late?

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:06.930
They ran into some trouble out in the field.

00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:10.760
They're on the way now, but it'll take another hour until they can make it. {keep this in mind as you see just how much they accomplish in the next scenes}

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:17.520
We can't just ask the audience to wait... What do you think, Kisaragi?

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:21.110
I'll do it.

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:24.150
I'll take the stage.

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:30.280
Sounds good to me. Put off the first-years' show and the three of us can hold the event!

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:31.790
That's not what I mean.

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:35.870
I'm saying I'll buy time until the girls can get here.

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:39.330
Huh, why? Kirara wants to be the star.

00:13:39.330 --> 00:13:41.630
If I can't be the star, then baa!

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:44.050
The spotlight belongs to them tonight.

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:49.760
Rola, I'll join in and help the first-years too.

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:51.180
Yume...

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:53.520
Tsubasa-senpai, do we have your permission?

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:58.150
Sakuraba, Nijino... I'll leave it to you.

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:00.270
What's with you?! That's boring!

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:03.070
If Kirara can't be the star, she's out!

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:05.440
It's fine, we'll deal with her later.

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:09.280
There's no time to waste. 
Let's get everything ready.

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:12.280
Yume, take care of the stage decorations.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:13.450
Okay!

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:15.660
I'll carry the equipment over.

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:16.910
Thank you.

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:23.500
<i>Still, I'm not sure we can make it with this few people.</i>

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:26.010
Sakuraba, I'm sorry, but if you could call the admins—

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:27.050
Already done.

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:29.800
They're on the way now.

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:36.680
I also asked the staff from our show to help out too.

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:40.020
You've grown dependable.

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:56.370
So boring...

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.750
Why are they trying so hard?

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:01.750
It's weird. {apparently Kirara is Mayu, not that you'd get that reference}

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:04.130
What song will you do?

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:06.840
Well, we were considering "STARDOM!". {technically STARDOM!}{or just roll with "STARDOM!.". you can't let a chance like this go to waste}

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:08.800
Sure, sounds good.

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:09.880
And your dresses?

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:12.260
I'll wear Spice Chord.

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:14.640
And I have Berry Parfait.

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:16.180
Then again...

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:20.890
We don't often get to be in a unit, 
so I'd like to wear matching dresses.

00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:26.110
Let's use our school dresses then! 
Today's stars are our first-years, after all.

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:27.280
Sure.

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:29.030
That sounds good.

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:34.030
We made it.

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:38.040
A crowd is starting to gather too.

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:41.290
Sakuraba, Nijino, it's all on you now.

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:42.250
Right!

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:50.380
Today's main program will be a concert held by Four Star Academy's first-years,

00:15:50.380 --> 00:15:53.140
but due to unforeseen circumstances, they'll be arriving late.

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:59.220
However, to tide you over under they get here,

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:03.850
Four Star Academy's Sakuraba Rola 
and S4's Nijino Yume will be performing.

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:12.240
Nijino Yume, ready to go!

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:16.120
Sakuraba Rola—It's our time to shine! {not sure if this is right, I"ll have to check}

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:46.450
They loved it!

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:47.990
We did it!

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:51.210
Your performance was really good.

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:54.130
But why are you giving it to the first-years now?

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:56.250
What do you mean, why?

00:19:56.250 --> 00:20:02.130
They've probably been doing everything they can, even sacrificing sleep to make this a success.

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:07.680
But Elza-sama always says in the world of idols, the weak are meat the strong do eat. {in this specific circumstance it's perfect, and apparantly an already existing translated idiom. perfect because of Elza's propensity for steak, that is}{some variant of dog-eat-dog world would probably have been naturaler, but I may this sore}

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:10.560
It's your own fault if you let a chance slip by.

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:17.230
Just keep it going! That's what anyone from Venus Ark would do.

00:20:20.070 --> 00:20:24.870
I don't know much about Elza-san or Venus Ark's philosophy.

00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:30.870
But I want to be an idol who's considerate of others and always willing to extend a helping hand.

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:33.000
Same with me.

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:40.010
I'm so sorry we're late!

00:20:40.010 --> 00:20:42.510
Senpai, thank you for holding out!

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:44.090
We've been waiting!

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:45.470
Hurry up and get ready!

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:46.010
Yes!

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:50.850
I don't get it. It's so weird... {I got distracted apparently}

00:20:50.850 --> 00:20:51.980
Kirara-chan.

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:55.020
Mind helping out?

00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:02.860
Geez, if you want me <i>that</i> much...

00:21:09.990 --> 00:21:13.160
Nijino and Sakuraba saved our necks there. {come on, you can't say Rola's name first this time? it's her episode}{lexigraphical order}

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:18.670
I know. Now that the event's up 
and running, I have nothing tying me back.

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:21.550
Have you made up your mind?

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:27.340
Yes. After consulting Momoko-sensei, I decided to go to Hollywood.

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:31.310
I see. But what about your brand?

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:37.270
Spice Chord is a brand with a reputation for being resolute and unshakable.

00:21:37.270 --> 00:21:40.360
Only those with a strong sense of responsibility can lead it.

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:44.150
I can't imagine anyone more suited for the position than you.

00:21:44.820 --> 00:21:48.700
I felt the same way... until today.

00:21:58.380 --> 00:22:00.340
That concludes Yume,

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:01.210
Rola,

00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:02.550
and Kirara's...

00:22:02.550 --> 00:22:05.630
It's the weekend! Where to?

00:22:05.630 --> 00:22:09.550
Today we took you on a tour of Kirakira City's popular spots.

00:22:09.550 --> 00:22:12.310
Have you decided where to go this weekend?

00:22:12.310 --> 00:22:14.810
Every place was super fun! {goddammit, it's probably her thing. I"m thinking super/super duper}{that's probably how I would translate it normally, so yes}

00:22:14.810 --> 00:22:17.520
Let's wrap this up. One, two...

00:22:17.520 --> 00:22:19.060
See you again!

00:22:19.060 --> 00:22:22.070
Cut! Okay, nice!

00:23:55.700 --> 00:23:59.500
My new school dress is the Blue Marching Coord.

00:23:59.500 --> 00:24:04.250
The rock bits splashed onto the design shout out your individuality.

00:24:04.250 --> 00:24:06.040
The key point is the choker.

00:24:06.040 --> 00:24:10.010
Wearing this dress makes me want to keep working hard at my Aikatsu tomorrow!

00:24:10.670 --> 00:24:12.720
It's this year's Koukadou audition! {I assume this is what it was}{I don't remember}

00:24:12.720 --> 00:24:15.510
Wait, what?! Elza-san's our rival?!

00:24:15.510 --> 00:24:18.350
No way... has she come to steal the throne of Felicitaiyaki?!

00:24:18.720 --> 00:24:20.480
Next time on Aikatsu Stars!

00:24:20.480 --> 00:24:21.680
Miracle Audition!

00:24:22.020 --> 00:24:24.310
Become the first-star idol!
